<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gwalior Fort</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gopachal, Gopadri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gwalior Fort is a hill fort above the city of Gwalior in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, one of the strongest fortresses of northern India. Held by successive dynasties, including the Kachchhapaghatas and Tomaras, it contains the Teli ka Mandir and Sas-Bahu temples, Jain rock-cut sculptures and the 15th-century Man Mandir palace. A temple inscription of 876 shows one of the earliest written zeros.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gwalior-fort.jpg" alt="Gwalior Fort" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anuppyr007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwalior_Fort_front.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
